## Context
DESIGN.md §4 PR-9, honoring D3 in the contained scope the derivation critique
forced (M3): upstream's one global embedderId cannot support mixed spaces, so
the small PR is keep-vectors + pin the query-side embedder to the stored
vectorEmbedderId until a rebuild switches both. The verified violation dies:
dropStaleVectors -> clearVectors() at open silently zeroes semantic coverage
on any model change. Dual-embed migration stays in the RFC (0027). Failing
test: open a db under a different ZOTEUS_EMBEDDING_MODEL, watch semantic
coverage survive.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] vectors survive a model switch; query embedder pinned to stored id
- [ ] coverage/status names the pinned model
- [ ] PR opened upstream; outcome recorded here

## Amendments (implementation review, 2026-08-26)
The violation has TWO sites, both to neuter: reconcileVectorProvenance ->
dropStaleVectors -> clearVectors() at open (index-manager.ts:286-308), and the
query-time dimension check that drops again (:889-892). "Pin" = construct the
provider from the stored identity string (name:model, embeddings.ts:29-31);
same-provider model pins are clean, and the PR must specify the cross-provider
degradation when the old provider is unconstructible (serve keyword + typed
reason, never drop). Political review (finding 4): the body must present the
failing test as a regression-in-effect and name the alternative reading —
dropStaleVectors was written on purpose.
